{"event":"step_update","step_update":{"conversation_id":"9bd3d3f3-d089-4779-9e01-3d72ce9fb75b","step_index":12,"state":"DONE","step_type":"tool","tool_name":"run_command","duration_seconds":0.08083,"tool_info":{"name":"run_command","parameters":{"CommandLine":"cat site/index.html site/app.js site/robots.txt api/routes.md"},"output":"\u003c!doctype html\u003e\r\n\u003chtml lang=\"en\"\u003e\r\n\u003chead\u003e\r\n\u003cmeta charset=\"utf-8\"\u003e\r\n\u003ctitle\u003eField notes\u003c/title\u003e\r\n\u003cmeta name=\"robots\" content=\"index,follow\"\u003e\r\n\u003clink rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"/styles.css\"\u003e\r\n\u003c/head\u003e\r\n\u003cbody\u003e\r\n\u003cheader\u003e\u003ca href=\"/\"\u003eField notes\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/header\u003e\r\n\u003cmain id=\"app\"\u003e\u003cp class=\"loading\"\u003eLoading…\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/main\u003e\r\n\u003cscript src=\"/app.js\"\u003e\u003c/script\u003e\r\n\u003c/body\u003e\r\n\u003c/html\u003e\r\n// Renders the home list or one note, depending on the path.\r\n(async function () {\r\n  const app = document.getElementById(\"app\");\r\n  const m = location.pathname.match(/^\\/n\\/([a-z0-9-]+)$/);\r\n  try {\r\n    if (m) {\r\n      const r = await fetch(`/v1/notes/${m[1]}`);\r\n      if (!r.ok) throw new Error(`HTTP ${r.status}`);\r\n      const note = await r.json();\r\n      document.title = `${note.title} · Field notes`;\r\n      app.innerHTML = `\u003carticle\u003e\u003ch1\u003e${esc(note.title)}\u003c/h1\u003e\u003cp class=\"meta\"\u003e${esc(note.date)}\u003c/p\u003e${note.html}\u003c/article\u003e`;\r\n    } else {\r\n      const r = await fetch(\"/v1/notes?limit=50\");\r\n      if (!r.ok) throw new Error(`HTTP ${r.status}`);\r\n      const notes = await r.json();\r\n      app.innerHTML = \"\u003cul\u003e\" + notes.map(n =\u003e `\u003cli\u003e\u003ca href=\"/n/${n.slug}\"\u003e${esc(n.title)}\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e`).join(\"\") + \"\u003c/ul\u003e\";\r\n    }\r\n  } catch (e) {\r\n    app.innerHTML = `\u003csection class=\"notfound\"\u003e\u003ch1\u003eNOT FOUND\u003c/h1\u003e\u003cp\u003eNo note lives at this address.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href=\"/\"\u003eBack to all notes\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/section\u003e`;\r\n  }\r\n  function esc(s) { return String(s).replace(/[\u0026\u003c\u003e\"]/g, c =\u003e ({\"\u0026\":\"\u0026amp;\",\"\u003c\":\"\u0026lt;\",\"\u003e\":\"\u0026gt;\",'\"':\"\u0026quot;\"}[c])); }\r\n})();\r\nUser-agent: *\r\nDisallow: /v1/\r\nDisallow: /admin/\r\n\r\nSitemap: https://fieldnotes.example/sitemap.xml\r\n# API routes (all under /v1/, same domain as the site)\r\n\r\n| Method | Path | Auth | Purpose |\r\n|---|---|---|---|\r\n| GET | /v1/notes | none | list public notes (`?limit=`) |\r\n| GET | /v1/notes/{slug} | none | one public note (JSON with `html`) |\r\n| POST | /v1/notes | bearer | create a note |\r\n| PUT | /v1/notes/{slug} | bearer | edit a note |\r\n| POST | /v1/notes/{slug}/reactions | bearer | react (per user) |\r\n| GET | /v1/me | bearer | the signed-in user |\r\n| GET | /v1/me/drafts | bearer | the user's drafts |\r\n| POST | /v1/auth/token | none | sign-in exchange |\r\n\r\nUnauthenticated POST/PUT return 401. Crawlers hitting POST-only paths with GET\r\nwere logging 404s and 405s all September, which is why `/v1/` was added to\r\nrobots.txt on 2026-09-07.\r\n"}}}
