{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"9bd3d3f3-d089-4779-9e01-3d72ce9fb75b","status":"SUCCESS","response":"The cause of the Soft 404 issue and the fix have been documented in [ANSWER.md](file:///tmp/h-NnLOJp/ANSWER.md), and [site/robots.txt](file:///tmp/h-NnLOJp/site/robots.txt) has been updated.\n\n### Summary\n\n- **Cause**:\n  The frontend is a single HTML shell (`site/index.html`) that fetches note data client-side via JavaScript (`site/app.js`) from `/v1/notes/{slug}`. When `Disallow: /v1/` was added to `site/robots.txt` in September, Googlebot respected the disallow rule when fetching subresources during rendering. Because the fetch failed, `app.js` rendered its fallback error UI: `\"NOT FOUND No note lives at this address.\"` Served with HTTP 200, this \"not found\" page was classified by Google Search Console as a Soft 404.\n\n- **Fix**:\n  Updated [site/robots.txt](file:///tmp/h-NnLOJp/site/robots.txt) to explicitly allow public note endpoints while blocking mutation and private endpoints using Google's longest-matching-rule logic:\n  ```txt\n  User-agent: *\n  Allow: /v1/notes\n  Disallow: /v1/notes/*/reactions\n  Disallow: /v1/\n  Disallow: /admin/\n\n  Sitemap: https://fieldnotes.example/sitemap.xml\n  ```\n","duration_seconds":56.01374,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":130939,"output_tokens":2607,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":132884,"total_tokens":133546}}}
